citi-rewards.l4:1684:1-1710:52:
  `Rate answer` OF 10, 0.4, Unconfirmed, 4, 4, 4, FALSE, TRUE, (Cap OF "Citi Rewards 10X bonus (statement month)", TRUE, 1000, `Statement month`, `By posting date`), (LIST "the 9 bonus points per S$1 stop after 9,000 Bonus Points in the statement month, about S$1,000 of 10X spend", "clause 5 also excludes GST, and bill payments made through a channel or agent other than internet banking; the statement line does not distinguish either", "five descriptions on Citibank's list — SAM, SPL AUTO*, SPL ATU*, SPL ONLINE* and TL-ABT — are not recognised by the statement-line classifier as it prints them, so a charge bearing one of them is not caught here"), (LIST Provenance OF "citi-rewards-10x-tnc", "6(i)", "Effective 1 April 2024", (DATE OF 1, 4, 2024), "a Qualifying Charge made at any store that sells shoes and bags and clothes as its main business activity, determined by the following Merchant Category Codes (MCC)", Provenance OF "citi-rewards-10x-tnc", "6(ii)", "Effective 1 April 2024", (DATE OF 1, 4, 2024), "a Qualifying Charge made at an online retail merchant, excluding mobile wallet and travel-related transactions*. These refer to Qualifying Charges made via the internet or mobile applications, which is determined by system indicators reflecting that it is an online transaction ... These indicators are decided by the relevant merchant and/or their acquirer and are not determined by Citibank.", Provenance OF "citi-rewards-10x-tnc", "6, footnote *", "Effective 1 April 2024", (DATE OF 1, 4, 2024), "For clarity, travel-related transactions refer to transactions which are either wholly or partially related to any form of travel, whether local or overseas and include but are not limited to transactions that fall within the following MCCs (i.e. any transactions at merchants with the following MCCs will not be a 10X Points Eligible Transaction)", Provenance OF "citi-rewards-10x-tnc", "13", "Effective 1 April 2024", (DATE OF 1, 4, 2024), "For every 10X Points Eligible Transaction charged to the Eligible Card, an Eligible Cardholder will be awarded: (i) 1 Base Point for every S$1 of a 10X Points Eligible Transaction (“Base Points”); and (ii) 9 Bonus Points for every S$1 of a 10X Points Eligible Transaction (“Bonus Points”). ... Base Points are not subject to any cap. However, Bonus Points are subject to a cap of 9,000 Bonus Points per statement month.", Provenance OF "citi-rewards-10x-tnc", "18", "Effective 1 April 2024", (DATE OF 1, 4, 2024), "Points reversal will be applied in the statement cycle when the reversal/refunded transaction is posted which may differ from the statement cycle of corresponding Qualifying Charge"), Verified
citi-rewards.l4:1715:1-1741:52:
  `Rate answer` OF 0, 0.4, Unconfirmed, 0, 0, 0, FALSE, FALSE, (Cap OF "Citi Rewards 10X bonus (statement month)", FALSE, 0, `Statement month`, `By posting date`), (LIST "this posting is a fee, an interest charge, an instalment plan, a transfer, a cash advance or a bill payment, so clause 5 makes it a non-qualifying charge and it earns no ThankYou Points at all"), (LIST Provenance OF "citi-rewards-10x-tnc", "5", "Effective 1 April 2024", (DATE OF 1, 4, 2024), "“Qualifying Charge” means a charge made to an Eligible Card which does not arise from any: (i) annual fees, interest charges, late payment charges, GST, cash advances, instalment/easy/extended/equal payment plans, preferred payment plans, balance transfers, cash advances, quasi-cash transactions, all fees charged by Citibank or third party, miscellaneous charges imposed by Citibank"), Verified
